$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
2-bromobiaryls S1a-S1q (GP1) Potassium carbonate (2.5 eq.), arylboronic
acid (1.1 eq.) and bis(triphenylphospine)palladium(II) dichloride were
added to a solution of 1-bromo-2-iodoarene (1.0 eq.) in a 15:2 solvent
mixture of DME and water (0.3 M). The reaction mixture was heated to 80
°C and stirred at this temperature until complete consumption of
1-bromo-2-iodoarene was observed (monitored by TLC, ~5 h). After cooling
to room temperature the mixture was diluted with a mixture of
diethylether (DEE) and water and the aqueous layer was extracted with DEE
(3 × 20 mL). After drying over MgSO4 and filtration the solvent was
evaporated in vacuo. The residue was purified by FC (P or P/EtOAc). The
desired 2-bromobiaryl S1 in 39-70% yield. 2-Bromo-4'-methyl-1,1'-biphenyl
(S1a) According to GP1 with 1-bromo-2-iodobenzene (1.2 mL, 9.3 mmol, 1.0
eq.), 4-methylphenylboronic acid (1.284 g, 9.44 mmol, 1.0 eq.), K2CO3
(3.123 g, 22.6 mmol, 2.4 eq.) and Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (98 mg, 0.14 mmol, 1.5 mol
%). 2-Bromo-5-methoxy-1,1'-biphenyl (S1k) According to GP1 with
1-bromo-2-iodo-4-methoxybenzene (1.096 g, 3.50 mmol, 1.0 eq.),
phenylboronic acid (451 mg, 3.70 mmol, 1.1 eq.), K2CO3 (1.209 g, 8.73
mmol, 2.5 eq.) and Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (38 mg, 54 μmol, 1.5 mol %). FC (P)
afforded the desired 2-bromobiaryl S1k (580 mg, 2.20 mmol, 63%, purity:
96%) as colorless liquid. 1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, 300 K): δ (ppm) = 7.55
(d, J = 8.7 Hz, 1H, CaromH), 7.46 – 7.38 (m, 5H, CaromH), 6.89 (d, J =
3.1 Hz, 1H, CaromH), 6.79 (dd, J = 8.8 Hz, J = 3.1 Hz, 1H, CaromH), 3.81
(s, 3H, CH3). 13C-NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3, 300 K): δ (ppm) = 158.8 (C), 143.4
(C), 141.2 (C), 133.7 (CH), 129.3 (2 × CH), 128.0 (2 × CH), 127.6 (CH),
116.7 (CH), 114.7 (CH), 113.1 (C), 55.5 (CH3). HRMS (APCI) m/z =
261.99878 calcd. for C13H11BrO [M]+, found: 261.99885. Spectroscopic data
are in accordance with those described in the literature.[6]
